Concept Application of Bootstrap in Startup Website Development
1. How Bootstrap’s Grid System Helps Build Layouts Faster Compared to Plain CSS
Bootstrap provides a responsive 12-column grid system that helps developers create website layouts quickly and efficiently.
In plain CSS, developers usually need to:
•	Write custom width values 
•	Use Flexbox or floats manually 
•	Create media queries for responsiveness 
•	Handle spacing and alignment separately 
This takes more time and increases complexity.
________________________________________
Bootstrap Grid Structure
Bootstrap uses:
container → row → columns
Example
<div class="container">
   <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-6">Left Section</div>
      <div class="col-md-6">Right Section</div>
   </div>
</div>
Explanation
•	container keeps content aligned properly. 
•	row creates a horizontal section. 
•	col-md-6 divides the page into equal halves. 
________________________________________
Benefits Over Plain CSS
1. Faster Development
Developers only add classes instead of writing lengthy CSS.
2. Automatic Responsiveness
The layout automatically adjusts for:
•	Mobile phones 
•	Tablets 
•	Desktops 
3. Less Code
No need for custom:
•	Width calculations 
•	Float handling 
•	Media queries 
4. Better Consistency
All sections maintain equal spacing and alignment.
Example in Plain CSS
.left {
   width: 50%;
   float: left;
}

.right {
   width: 50%;
   float: right;
}
Bootstrap replaces this with:
<div class="col-md-6"></div>
Thus, Bootstrap significantly speeds up UI creation while keeping the design professional.
