3. How Responsive Utility Classes and Breakpoints Handle Device Compatibility
Modern websites must work properly on:
•	Smartphones 
•	Tablets 
•	Laptops 
•	Large desktop screens 
Bootstrap handles this using:
1.	Breakpoints 
2.	Responsive utility classes 
________________________________________
Breakpoints in Bootstrap
Bootstrap defines screen sizes using breakpoints.
Breakpoint	Device
sm	Small devices
md	Tablets
lg	Laptops
xl	Large screens
________________________________________
Example
<div class="col-12 col-md-6 col-lg-4">
Meaning
•	col-12 → Full width on mobile 
•	col-md-6 → Half width on tablet 
•	col-lg-4 → One-third width on desktop 
The layout automatically changes according to screen size.
________________________________________
Responsive Utility Classes
Bootstrap utility classes quickly control:
•	Display 
•	Alignment 
•	Margin 
•	Padding 
•	Visibility 
Examples
Class	Purpose
text-centre	Centres text
d-none	Hides element
p-3	Padding
m-2	Margin
________________________________________
Device-Specific Utilities
Example:
<div class="d-none d-md-block">
Meaning:
•	Hidden on mobile 
•	Visible on tablets and desktops 
________________________________________
Advantages
•	No manual media queries needed 
•	Faster responsive design 
•	Better user experience 
•	Cleaner code 
This ensures the startup website works smoothly on all devices.
