6. How This Page Can Later Be Converted into React or Angular UI
Modern frontend frameworks like:
•	React 
•	Angular 
use a component-based architecture.
Bootstrap layouts can easily be reused inside these frameworks.
________________________________________
Component-Based Conversion
Each Bootstrap section can become a reusable component.
Example:
•	Navbar → Navbar Component 
•	Service Card → Card Component 
•	Footer → Footer Component 
________________________________________
Example in React
function ServiceCard() {
  return (
    <div className="card">
       <div className="card-body">
          <h5>Web Development</h5>
          <p>Responsive websites for startups.</p>
       </div>
    </div>
  );
}
________________________________________
Example in Angular
<app-service-card></app-service-card>
Angular separates:
•	HTML templates 
•	TypeScript logic 
•	CSS styling 
________________________________________
Benefits of Conversion
1. Reusable Components
One component can be used multiple times.
________________________________________
2. Easier Maintenance
Updating one component updates all instances.
________________________________________
3. Dynamic Content Handling
React and Angular can fetch:
•	API data 
•	User data 
•	Database content 
without reloading the page.
________________________________________
4. Better Performance
Modern frameworks improve:
•	Rendering speed 
•	State management 
•	User interaction 
________________________________________
5. Scalability
The startup can later expand features such as:
•	Login systems 
•	Dashboards 
•	Payment systems 
•	Real-time notifications 
